<title>POLAND: Polish Jan-Feb customs trade gap at $2.354 bln.</title>
<headline>Polish Jan-Feb customs trade gap at $2.354 bln.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's registered trade gap in the January-February period was $2.354 billion, against a $1.482 billion deficit in the same period of 1996, the Central Statistical Office said (GUS).</p>
<p>GUS said exports grew 3.4 percent and imports 18.8 percent in the first two months of 1997 against the same pariod of 1996.</p>
<p> POLISH TRADE (USD bln)     JAN-FEB 1997	 JAN-FEB 1996</p>
<p> Trade balance		     2.354		   1.482</p>
<p> exports			     3.990		   3.858</p>
<p> imports			     6.344		   5.340</p>
<p> TRADE WITH EU		  JAN-FEB 1997	 JAN-FEB 1996</p>
<p> Trade balance		     1.379		   0.781</p>
<p> exports			     2.693		   2.635</p>
<p> imports			     4.072		   3.416</p>
<p>NOTE - GUS trade data differs from data reported by the National Bank of Poland (the central bank) because GUS bases figures on customs receipts while the NBP reports cash flows.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
